@startuml seq_scraper_chase
title contrai-scraper — one chase, lobby to record (Worker._hall → Recorder.run with a target)

' --- Palette: scraper purple, with contrai-data teal for the record end ---
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #5E4495
    LifeLineBorderColor #9B7FCC
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #EDE7F6
    ParticipantBorderColor #5E4495
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #EDE7F6
    ParticipantFontColor #311B92
    ActorBorderColor #5E4495
    ActorBackgroundColor #EDE7F6
    ActorFontColor #311B92
    GroupBorderColor #5E4495
    GroupBackgroundColor #F3E5F5
    GroupHeaderFontColor #311B92
    BoxBorderColor #5E4495
    BoxBackgroundColor #F3E5F5
    DividerBorderColor #5E4495
    DividerBackgroundColor #D1C4E9
    DividerFontColor #311B92
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
    BorderColor #F9A825
    FontColor #5F4B00
}

box "one worker" #F3E5F5
    participant "Worker\n(fleet.py)" as W <<scraper>>
    participant "Spectator\n(browser.py)" as SP <<scraper>>
    participant "page\n(its own context)" as PG
    participant "frames\n+ WireStream" as FS <<scraper>>
    participant "LobbyWatcher\n(lobby.py)" as LW <<scraper>>
    participant "Recorder\n(target set)" as R <<scraper>>
end box

box "shared by the fleet" #EDE7F6
    participant "TableRegistry\n(registry.py)" as REG <<scraper>>
end box

participant "RecordWriter" as RW <<from contrai-data>> #E0F5F2

== 0. In the lobby ==

W -> SP : log_in(), enter_lobby()
SP -> PG : online · new games · the variant
SP -> PG : what is under the centre?
note right of SP
  The first-visit overlay goes at any click,
  but without it a click at the centre sits
  the account down at a table slot: so the
  click is made only when the list is not
  what lies under it.
end note
W -> SP : read_tournament_hash()
SP --> W : the tournament row's hash
note right of W
  Read off the page once. The socket
  says everything about a row except
  which one is the tournament's.
end note

loop until the tournament row raises its **full** flag
    FS -> LW : lobby_table event
    LW -> LW : seats = this event's whole map
end
LW --> W : LobbyRoster(seats, at) · named by its digest
note right of LW
  Never merged with the last event: nothing
  vacates a seat on the wire, so adding events
  up leaves ghosts and invents rosters that
  never sat together.
end note

alt older than ""roster_max_age_s""
    W -> W : roster_stale, and keep waiting
else another worker read it first
    W -> REG : claim_roster(accounts)
    REG --> W : refused · roster_taken, and keep waiting
else claimed
    W -> REG : claim_roster(accounts)
    REG --> W : granted

    == 1. Out to a table ==

    W -> SP : enter_table_from_lobby()
    loop back, until observe is in reach
        SP -> PG : read every back control and its screen's style
        SP -> PG : click the best-ranked one on the screen shown
    end
    SP -> PG : observe · the variant
    W -> R : Recorder(target = ChaseTarget, claims).run()
    activate R

    == 2. The blind scan ==

    loop until the table is found, ""distinct_budget"" tables are judged, or ""scan_deadline_s"" passes
        FS -> R : a join snapshot · not the table just left
        R -> REG : seen(table) · into the census
        R -> REG : holder(table)
        alt another worker is watching it
            R -> SP : next_table() · claimed_by_other
        else fewer than four of the roster's accounts
            R -> SP : next_table() · roster_mismatch, how many matched
        else all four
            R -> R : chase_matched · distinct tables, seconds since the roster
        end
    end

    == 3. The table ==

    R -> SP : read_options(), read_scoreboard()
    note right of R
      Every gate a table meets under ""run""
      still applies: a chase is not a way
      round the tournament, options or
      orientation checks.
    end note
    R -> REG : claim_table(table) · atomic, on acceptance
    note right of REG
      Claimed only now, not on arrival: a scan
      passing through a table never holds it,
      so it never keeps out the worker that
      came to find it.
    end note
    loop the game, refreshing the claim on every frame
        FS -> R : WireEvent
    end
    R -> R : split_visits(buffer) · one game, one table?
    R -> RW : one record · game_recorded carries first_round
    R -> REG : release_table(table)
    R --> W : SessionSummary · chase_ended or chase_gave_up
    deactivate R
    W -> REG : release_roster(accounts)

    == 4. Back to the lobby ==

    W -> SP : return_to_lobby()
    opt a table is showing, and the profile names table_exit
        SP -> PG : reveal the rail · the table's exit\nlands on the online menu
    end
    alt a step does not land
        W -> W : return_rebuilt · a fresh session, no budget spent
    else
        SP -> PG : back until new games is in reach · the variant
    end
end

@enduml
